# Normalize all text files to LF line endings on checkout, regardless of
# platform or the developer's core.autocrlf setting. Without this, Windows
# checkouts (core.autocrlf=true, which is the Git for Windows default) convert
# .cs files to CRLF. Several Roslyn code fix provider tests embed expected
# output in C# raw string literals, whose line endings are the literal source
# file's physical line endings rather than something the compiler normalizes.
# The code fix providers themselves always emit LF-only output (see
# BiDiDriver008_UnsafeEvaluateResultCastCodeFixProvider.cs and the
# SyntaxFactory.ElasticLineFeed usages across the other providers), so a CRLF
# checkout makes the expected and actual text mismatch only on Windows.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit binary types, to avoid relying on Git's content-based detection.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.snk binary
